========================================================================
PLAIN ENGLISH (RULES 1.10)
========================================================================

**What changed**
Process helpers that start or stop programs now ask for a smaller
permission token (`ProcessCap`) instead of the broad OS token (`SysCap`).
That matches the rule already used at compile time for spawn and exec.

**Why it matters**
Callers can grant only “run a process,” not full OS control.
The AI/python bridge still needs the broad OS token on purpose.

**What still is not done**
Many domain libraries still pass the broad OS token (~571 places).
That bulk is named residual, not cleaned up in this wave.
Full OS isolation is not claimed.

**What to do next (if anything)**
Optional later waves: domain SysCap stubs where a sealed process op exists.
Do not move python_embed to ProcessCap.
Human gate for push. Docs Cartographer does not push.

